data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11, the **sync-over-async opt-in for the Cosmos DB provider is removed**. The synchronous LINQ operators (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`) and `SaveChanges()` will throw `InvalidOperationException` unconditionally — there's no configuration to re-enable them.

The Cosmos DB SDK is inherently async, so EF Core is dropping the sync-over-async shim entirely.

## Fix: Convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key changes:**
- Return `Task<T>` / `Task` instead of bare types
- Use `ToListAsync()`, `FirstAsync()`, `CountAsync()`, `SaveChangesAsync()`
- Callers must `await` these methods (async propagates up the call stack)

You'll also need to remove your old `EnableSyncOverAsync()` / `AllowSynchronousIO` configuration — it will cause a build warning or no-op in EF Core 11.
